{"kind":"report","text":"Planner decision for 31fcbdea (G1 remaining boundaries).\n\n(1) Overview continuity: one joint path. Replace the developer Directory root in the operator harness with genuine owned descendant selection, the M2b form, so the operator's path runs Site to Room to the alert through the same install the demo will use. Do not fabricate a LaneRef. Qualify nothing.\n\n(2) Manual zone controls: extend the generic form, not a native act wrapper. A declared act on a card may carry constant arguments declared in the view description and bound at declaration, never typed by the model: the heater card is a device record whose two acts are set-heater with the declared constant level values, and set-vent likewise on a vent record. A zone record links to its device records (card navigation, the Back direction of the kit), so the zone card itself declares no act on another item. The bounds hold per card: at most two acts, same item, and the act names stay native. Surface resources keep no signing controls. The view-description text in the grow note's 6.2 gains the constant-argument form when the note is next amended; implement from this decision now and name it in G1's implementation note.\n\n(3) Zone sparkline: a bounded generic series declaration on a record: the source projection (the journal log of readings), the field, the window (the last N rows, N at most 64), rendered from the native integers with the field's scale and unit descriptor and each row's source time; no invented samples, joins or smoothing; the fallback text gives latest, lowest and highest with their times. If this exceeds G1's two days, it is the last item and may ship as a second G1 head.\n\nContinue S1 meanwhile; none of this blocks it."}